This image illustrates the in vivo biodistribution and clearance of Nano-11 nanoparticles over time following intramuscular injection. Whole-mouse imaging (A) shows that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 remains localized at the injection site in the hind legs and gradually clears over a 21-day period. Excised organs (B) confirm that Nano-11 does not distribute systemically to internal organs. Quantification of fluorescence intensity at the injection site (C) reveals an initial rapid decrease, a subsequent increase by day 2, and then a continuous decline, with approximately 20% of the initial signal remaining after 21 days.